From a6fb896849f15b62a87087cd1699c292e8007396 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ariel Peretz <benoit.casse@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rumpnet: link the pcn driver (AMD PCnet) too, not only wm
To: bug-hurd@gnu.org

RUMPLIBS only pulls in rumpdev_pci_if_wm, so rumpnet can attach a wm
device and nothing else, even though the rump kernel tree ships the pcn
driver as well (sys/rump/dev/lib/libpci_if_pcn, library rumpdev_pci_if_pcn).

No interface name is hardcoded anywhere in rumpnet: the if_* drivers
attach through the rump autoconf machinery, so linking the extra
library is all that is needed to make AMD PCnet cards usable.

This is what QEMU's -device pcnet (the default on some machines and the
model used by the Hurd test setups) needs.

Keep wm first: it stays the default driver, this only adds a second one.
---
 rumpnet/Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rumpnet/Makefile b/rumpnet/Makefile
index 579197e1..60f6bd5c 100644
--- a/rumpnet/Makefile
+++ b/rumpnet/Makefile
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
 #   along with this program; if not, write to the Free Software
 #   Foundation, Inc., 675 Mass Ave, Cambridge, MA 02139, USA.
 
-RUMPLIBS=rump rumpuser rumpdev rumpdev_miiphy rumpdev_pci rumpvfs rumpdev_pci_if_wm rumpnet rumpnet_net rumpnet_netinet rumpnet_local rumpdev_bpf
+RUMPLIBS=rump rumpuser rumpdev rumpdev_miiphy rumpdev_pci rumpvfs rumpdev_pci_if_wm rumpdev_pci_if_pcn rumpnet rumpnet_net rumpnet_netinet rumpnet_local rumpdev_bpf
 # If we have a configured tree, include the configuration so that we
 # can conditionally build translators.
 ifneq (,$(wildcard ../config.make))
-- 
2.47.3

